                        "entry_id": "d56d6a3c-b4ce-30b2-b4cc-144f3ef84cb9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One of the poorer classes of Neapolitans; a chance-worker or beggar."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical",
                            "in-plural"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8a6aedc3-61ef-4c27-a1a0-7ba671b79e68",
                                "sense_id": "a451bd69-66c7-3107-a240-3371db2fed6e",
                                "text": "What does he mean by his Rights of Man, and his equality?—What wretched and dangerous doctrine to diſſeminate among the lazzaroni* of England, where they are always ready enough to murmur againſt their betters?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "592ff603-cd1f-42eb-afdf-d4c6a9384d27",
                                "sense_id": "a451bd69-66c7-3107-a240-3371db2fed6e",
                                "text": "[…] attended by one or two of his band, who intended leaving off business and turning lazzaroni, they all set off for Naples, which they found in an uproar."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e33f557e-f572-4fdd-b27a-d4b2c55c91d0",
                                "sense_id": "a451bd69-66c7-3107-a240-3371db2fed6e",
                                "text": "[…] Brighton, a clean Naples with genteel lazzaroni—[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7538abb2-6d37-475d-bbf7-c088640d0ff9",
                                "sense_id": "a451bd69-66c7-3107-a240-3371db2fed6e",
                                "text": "Marcher said to himself that he ought to have rendered her some service - saved her from a capsized boat in the bay, or at least recovered her dressing bag, filched from her cab, in the streets of Naples, by a lazzarone with a stiletto."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
